==Trivia==
*The Firecracker's weapon resembles [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shoulder-fired_missile man-portable rocket launchers]. Rocket Launchers were first developed in ancient China in the ninth century. Originally, they were firing multiple arrows together in a device called [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fire_arrow fire arrow], until they were replaced with rocket motors during the twelfth century.
**In the Turkish and Portuguese language settings of the game, the Firecracker's name translates to "Pyrotechnist". In the Dutch and Indonesian language settings of the game, the Firecracker's name translates to "Fireworks Shooter". In the French, Spanish, Italian, Japanese, Korean, Russian, Arabic, Chinese, Malaysian, Thai, and Finnish language settings of the game, the Firecracker's name translates to "Artificer", "Firethrower", "Pyrotechnic Archer", "Rocket Gunner", "Rocketeer", "Fire Archer", "Fireworks Thrower", "Fireworks Gunner", "Firecracker Shooter", "Firework Archer", and "Firewoman" respectively.
**The Firecracker is 1 of 5 [[cards]] associated with rocketry, with the others being [[Rocket]], [[Goblin Machine]], [[Party Rocket]], and [[Rocket Silo]].
**According to a [https://x.com/Seth_Supercell/status/1212713267543576577?s=20 tweet], the Firecracker's firework is taken from an Air Defense from Clash of Clans. Additionally, the rocket shot by the Goblin Machine resembles the Firecracker’s firework.
*The Firecracker was inspired by [https://brawlstars.fandom.com/wiki/Penny Penny] from Brawl Stars, another Supercell game, according to  [https://youtu.be/DMi-5WpqQHk?t=53 Firecracker's intro video].
*The Firecracker is 1 of 17 [[:Category:Troop Cards|troops]] that inspired a troop in Clash of Clans, the others being [[Spear Goblins]], [[Bomber]], [[Bats]], [[Skeleton Barrel]], [[Minion Horde]], [[Battle Ram]], [[Ice Golem]], [[Zappies]], [[Baby Dragon]], [[Giant Skeleton]], [[Ram Rider]], [[Inferno Dragon]], [[Miner]], [[Royal Ghost]], [[Ice Wizard]], and [[Night Witch]].
*The Firecracker is one of the first troop cards to receive a [[Card Evolution]], alongside the [[Skeletons]], [[Barbarians]], and [[Royal Giant]].
*The Firecracker is 1 of 4 troops which can defeat itself in one attack, the others being Skeletons, Bats and [[Wall Breakers]].
*The Firecracker is 1 of 3 troops to recoil when attacking, the others being [[Sparky]] and [[Super Archers]].
*The Firecracker is 1 of 23 troops that has been featured in the [[Troop Rush]] game [[:Category:Modes|mode]], the others being Skeletons, [[Skeleton Dragons]], [[Fire Spirit]], Bats, [[Elite Barbarians]], [[Rascals|Rascal Girls]], [[Royal Hogs]], [[Heal Spirit]], [[Elixir Golem]], [[Guards]], [[Prince]], [[Balloon]], [[Golem]], Wall Breakers, Ram Rider, Sparky, [[Phoenix]], Royal Ghost, [[Bandit]], [[Lumberjack]], [[Santa Hog Rider]], and the [[Monk]].
*From her description, it is implied that the Firecracker used to be an [[Archers|Archer]].
*Along with the Rascals, Magic Archer, Bandit, and the [[Boss Bandit]], the Firecracker belongs to the Forest Gang.
*If the Boss Bandit is played when an allied Firecracker is on the field, she says "''You fire, I dash!''".
*The spread angle between the leftmost and rightmost small projectiles is 70 degrees, which means the angle between any two adjacent small projectiles is 17.5 degrees.
*The Firecracker is the subject of 4 [[Emotes]].
**The Santa Firecracker Emote was originally going to appear in December of 2021, but did not make it to the game until the December of 2022.<br />

